time to get  cooking with nanny bubbe today she is  showing us how to make  a delicious beet salad welcome back  nanny bubbe i cannot wait to hear this  it sounds perfect for the summer time  doesn't it really but i've got it i've  got to tell you there's  tremendous feedback right now anyway  there  is um it is very i'm so sorry  i'm hearing myself come back into my own  ears and i'm losing my thoughts i  apologize  so let me just tell you that i had a  beet salad  in laguna beach and it was absolutely  amazing  and i absolutely wanted to do it but  beets seem so daunting to me they seem  like ecommerce  and it seems like you can actually like  cutting through the skin or cutting  through the meat is very very difficult  but i found out after this salad it was  so delicious  i really worked hard to figure out a  great recipe  and so here it is so the first thing i  want to tell you is to separate your red  beets from your golden beets it's very  important  and what i'm going to show you is as you  cut it off it starts bleeding all over  everything so you always want a piece  put a piece of parchment underneath it  and you always want to do your golden  beets before your red beets  and because if you don't see what  happens you will get your golden beets  pink  so we're gonna slice off the ends we are  going  to shave off the skin and one of the  most important things to tell you  is that if you put the entire bulb  into the pot to steam it will  automatically  make the outer part of the bulb very  very overdone and the inner part under  done  so you really want to dice it and or  slice it before you put it into the  steaming pot  and so i'm just going to show you really  quickly that we're going to  dice it whoop dicing it here  slicing and then some dicing real fast  and into the pot into the  silicone steaming basket  so i'll just take a handful and just  show you it goes right  in like that and then each piece will be  perfectly perfectly steamed  so the next step we're going to do is  we're going to be making whipped  rogue now two things about roper  roguefort comes  directly from roguefort branch in france  it cannot say rope for just like you  can't say champagne unless it comes from  champagne france  also it is a sheep's cheese it's not a  cow's milk cheese so if you're allergic  to cow's milk you  you can eat it which is great so we've  got  room temperature roquefort into the food  processor  about two tablespoons of marscapone  cheese  we're going to take a squeeze of lemon  juice  and a tablespoon of olive oil  into the pot do you like roquefort  mercedes  i'm contemplating all of this i love  that and i love it  okay this salad is only 10 ingredients  it sounds so extravagant  and we got this good for you yes it's  beautiful  thank you i can't wait to try this so  what you want to do is you want to  refrigerate this for about three  30 minutes to get a little bit hard  which i've already done  and i'm going to show you how to plate  this so the first thing we're going to  do  is we're going to take the arugula we  put a little bit of olive oil and lemon  juice onto the arugula already  so we're going to put a mound of it just  like that now you can either platter  plate this or individual plate it last  night for my husband's birthday i  individually plated it and we're going  to take a mound of the red  first right this red will go on the  bottom  just like this 10 ingredients good for  you  i was i never thought to count that but  that was a good call on your part i love  that but it's easy  yes and not not all food needs to be  easy because  sometimes easy isn't as healthy as you  would want so now you put your golden  beets right on top are you loving that  on top of that we are going to put  pistachio nuts just like this you see  that  now one of the other keys is taking a  little bit of french sea salt boy  everything is french i bet even beets  would be french but they're not i think  they're russian originated in russia  a little bit of french sea salt and now  the beet dust this is the key a  tablespoon of sugar  a teaspoon of beet powder  and it's just this little fairy dust  that you sprinkle  all over including on the side of the  plate  and then very quickly off with the  cheese  a little bit over here and a little bit  over here  which i almost forgot oh here we go  and just a little bit of beet powder on  those because it turns a little bit gray  and the beet powder brings it back  to blue and there you have it you love  that  beautiful summer salad i had no idea  that beet powder was a thing and like we  said  10 ingredients nanny bubbe you always  have  the best recipes that looks delicious  you can't be beat  up thank you you can't be beat  check out danny bubby's kitchen and  garden on social media and online at  nannybubby.com  thank you to chapman automotive for  sponsoring the segment las vegas now  we'll be right back

